# The ACCEPT side of the module-dict conditional-binding guard — ouroboros#141.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that a guard has two ways to be wrong and the
# refusal tier only gates one of them. The first version of this guard refused
# a module for having a `for` body (whose names never reach the dict) and for
# re-assigning a name it had already bound at the top level (where the dict is
# the same either way). Both are silent losses of reach, invisible to a suite
# that only checks that the bad case is refused.
#
# So: every shape the guard must ACCEPT, diffed against the VM.

import _t100mod
print of (keys of _t100mod)
print of _t100mod.a
print of _t100mod.b
print of _t100mod.u1
print of _t100mod.floop
print of (_t100mod.g of null)
